<rml>
	<head>
		<title>Launcher</title>
		<link type="text/rcss" href="rml.rcss"/>
		<link type="text/rcss" href="recomp.rcss"/>
		<style>
			body
			{
				width: 100%;
				height: 100%;
			}

			/* The launcher's cover art. These rules live here rather than in
			   recomp.rcss because that file is GENERATED from assets/scss by a
			   sass step that only runs under Windows' npm, so an edit there would
			   be overwritten by the next build and would not survive in the
			   source. They are launcher-only styling, so the document is the right
			   home for them either way.

			   The image is registered from C++ under the name below before this
			   document is created; see register_launcher_background in
			   src/ui/ui_launcher.cpp. The `?/` prefix is what stops RmlUi
			   resolving the name as a file path relative to this document, and
			   without it the renderer silently substitutes a 1x1 transparent
			   texture rather than reporting anything. */
			.launcher__backdrop
			{
				display: flex;
				position: absolute;
				top: 0;
				right: 0;
				bottom: 0;
				left: 0;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
				overflow: hidden;
			}

			/* Fitted to the WIDTH and centred. Fitting to the height instead would
			   cover the window whatever its shape, but only by cropping the sides
			   off — and the sides are where half the cast is.

			   The artist's painting is 3.1:1; the file here is 16:9, and the
			   difference is where the seam was. Left at 3.1:1 it sat in a band with
			   .launcher's #0D0A07 above and below, and the two blacks do not match:
			   the painting's top and bottom rows are a dark BLUE, about
			   rgb(10,11,30), against a warm near-black. No flat colour fixes that
			   either, because the painting's edge is pure black at the far left and
			   right and blue through the middle.

			   So the transition happens inside the image. Its own edge rows are
			   extended outward — smoothed horizontally first, since stretching a
			   single row leaves vertical streaks — and then faded into #0D0A07 over
			   the outer 230px, so the file's outermost rows ARE the launcher's
			   colour. Any band left at a window shape other than 16:9 is therefore
			   invisible. README.md carries the command that builds it. */
			.launcher__backdrop-art
			{
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
			}

			/* Readability. The menu column sits over the right-hand third of the
			   art, which is the busiest part of it. */
			.launcher__backdrop-scrim
			{
				position: absolute;
				top: 0;
				right: 0;
				bottom: 0;
				left: 0;
				background-color: rgba(13, 10, 7, 0.55);
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div id="window" data-model="launcher_model">
			<div class="launcher">
				<!-- The cover art, first child so everything below paints over it.
				     Goemon64Recomp puts its art in a .launcher__background-wrapper
				     inside the right-hand column, sized to the height and faded to
				     0.1 as a watermark behind the menu; this is a full-width
				     backdrop across the whole launcher instead, because the artwork
				     is a wide cast line-up rather than a single character.

				     Art by I_LIKE_SONIC. -->
				<div class="launcher__backdrop">
					<img class="launcher__backdrop-art" src="?/launcher/background"/>
					<div class="launcher__backdrop-scrim"></div>
				</div>

				<!-- One game, so one panel. Goemon64Recomp's launcher split the
				     screen in two because it offers Goemon's Great Adventure
				     alongside Mystical Ninja. The right-hand half is kept, because
				     that is the half recomp.rcss styles as the selected one; the
				     left is the empty column beside it. -->
				<div class="launcher__vertical-split">
					<div class="launcher__title-quadrant"></div>
					<div class="launcher__content-quadrant"></div>
				</div>
				<div class="launcher__vertical-split launcher__vertical-split--right">
					<div class="launcher__title-quadrant launcher__title-quadrant--right">
						<button class="subtitle-title subtitle-title--right" selected>
							<div><h3>Hybrid Heaven: Recompiled</h3></div>
							<div><h1>Hybrid Heaven</h1></div>
						</button>
					</div>
					<div class="launcher__content-quadrant">
						<button data-if="!rom_valid" onclick="select_rom" class="menu-list-item menu-list-item--right" autofocus>
							<div class="menu-list-item__bullet"></div>
							<div class="menu-list-item__label">Select ROM</div>
						</button>
						<button data-if="rom_valid" onclick="start_game" class="menu-list-item menu-list-item--right" autofocus>
							<div class="menu-list-item__bullet"></div>
							<div class="menu-list-item__label">Start Game</div>
						</button>
						<button onclick="open_controls" class="menu-list-item menu-list-item--right">
							<div class="menu-list-item__bullet"></div>
							<div class="menu-list-item__label">Controls</div>
						</button>
						<button onclick="open_settings" class="menu-list-item menu-list-item--right">
							<div class="menu-list-item__bullet"></div>
							<div class="menu-list-item__label">Settings</div>
						</button>
						<button onclick="open_mods" class="menu-list-item menu-list-item--right">
							<div class="menu-list-item__bullet"></div>
							<div class="menu-list-item__label">Mods</div>
						</button>
						<button onclick="exit_game" class="menu-list-item menu-list-item--right">
							<div class="menu-list-item__bullet"></div>
							<div class="menu-list-item__label">Exit</div>
						</button>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="bottom-left">
					<label>v{{version_number}}</label>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</body>
</rml>
